                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The controls are stiff and tank like, which are complemented by the terrible camera. Combat is shallow and uninteresting. Amounting to ‘click on an enemy until its dead’, and occasionally block a telegraphed attack. There is no indication of damage given or received outside of numbers. For some god forsaken reason the game interrupts combat with trivia of all things for a small buff. Everything looks like a generic royalty free asset, and the frames still chug at random times for seemingly no reason.\n\nThere is nothing interesting or worth your time or money in this game, look elsewhere.\n",
                        "timestamp_created": 1513919227,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1513919227,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 23,
                        "votes_funny": 1,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5588839054107666,
                        "comment_count": 12,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Some of the comments below are abusive. Notice user was/is part of \"National Bully Association\" group. \n\n\n>> We added CTRL or press right joystick for free camera\n>> This indie game is a mod from a arcade game. We apologize for the camera.\n\nHi, thank you for your feedback. \n\nThe questions are a bonus feature you can disable at any time. Did you try to disable it?  ---> Update: The EBS questions system is not active anymore.\n\nIt sounds like you need to play the game further to understand the concept.\n\nTalk to player \"Akbaar the great\" she had the same reaction and then started to understand the game and enjoyed it. \n\n0% of the graphics are from a asset store, they are all originals. Did you complete some quests? It starts by talking to the first guard.\n\nTo get more feedback from battles open the log ui (last button on your right). Its there for special players needs. There are 3 special move attacks you need to discover and special attacks with crystal dust. Did you find theses weapons?\n\nWe are sorry you did not enjoy the game.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1669734407,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": true
                    }
                ],
